      "source": "The following example calculates the remainder of dividing 8.625 by 0.75:",
      "normalizedSource": "The following example calculates the remainder of dividing 8.625 by 0.75:",
      "sourceHash": "7d9a4163de6afb135220d2ed364300b4c489b30a61f4dce0a4566262737286da",
      "translatable": true,
      "contextBefore": "Note that `q` is *not* `x / y` computed in floating-point arithmetic, and that `q` may not be representable in any available integer type.",
      "contextAfter": "```swift\nlet x = 8.625\nprint(x / 0.75)\n// Prints \"11.5\"\n\nlet q = (x / 0.75).rounded(.toNearestOrEven)\n// q == 12.0\nlet r = x.remainder(dividingBy: 0.75)\n// r == -0.375\n\nlet x1 = 0.75 * q + r\n// x1 == 8.625\n```",
